      "content": "Packets are generally routed as expected unless there's an issue with your client's Internet Service Provider (ISP) or the DNS server you're using. The intermittent issues some users are experiencing could be due to data being temporarily cached by intermediary DNS resolvers or ISPs, causing inconsistencies in what users' devices see. It might also be worth reaching out to your client's ISP to ensure they're not experiencing any problems with the routing or connectivity that could be affecting the DNS lookup for your site.",
