      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A traceroute can indeed provide valuable information about the path your DNS requests are taking to reach the server and where they might be encountering delays or issues. It can help determine if packets are getting stuck or rerouted unexpectedly. Share the output with your client for further investigation. Additionally, consider using tools like DNS monitoring services to get a clearer picture of the DNS resolution times across different geographical locations. This can also help pinpoint if the issue is localized or widespread.",
